WindowPane default update rate

Status: DONE
Milestone: Default to the highest selectable 60 fps target
Dependencies: 02_NATIVE_CAPTURE.todo, 03_DESKTOP_CONTROLS.todo
Purpose: Make the live pane update more frequently by default.

Tasks:
- [x] Support 1, 5, 10, 30 and 60 fps with a shared allowed-rate list.
- [x] Default the controls, timer and new capture sessions to 60 fps.
- [x] Use sub-millisecond capture-interval precision for 30/60 fps.
- [x] Qualify default selection and live changes through native handlers.
- [x] Refresh controls imagery, guides, ledger and owned continuity.

Acceptance criteria:
- New sessions select 60 fps; both 30/60 fps work during capture.
- Existing lower rates remain selectable; invalid selections report errors.
- Documentation distinguishes requested cadence from measured throughput.
- Historical 5 fps fixture observations are not relabeled as 60 fps results.

Completion evidence:
- Release /W4 /WX build passes 18 pure cases and 47 native checks.
- New-session controls select 60 fps. Actual 30/60 fps selection handlers
  retain active capture and deliver newly repainted synthetic source pixels.
- Optional native demo passes 46 checks; ordinary startup/tray/recovery/exit
  smoke passes. Refreshed controls screenshot visibly selects 60 fps / maximum.
- Formatting, whitespace, local documentation/media links and refreshed native
  GIF decoding pass. Resource fixture explicitly selects 5 fps, then restores
  60 fps; its results are not measurements of 60 fps throughput.
